{
  "title": "21: al-Anbiyaa الأنبياء",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِقْتَرَبَ لِلنَّاسِ حِسَابُهُمْ وَهُمْ فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(1)\nAEQTARABA LIN-NAASE HESAABUHUM WA HUM FEE GHAFLATIM MO’REZOON.\nHath drawn nigh unto the people (the day of) their reckoning, and they in heedlessness are turning aside.\nمَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ ذِكْرٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّہِمْ مُّحْدَثٍ اِلَّا اسْتَمَعُوْهُ وَهُمْ يَلْعَبُوْنَۙ‏(2)\nMAA YAATEEHIM MIN ZEKRIN MIN RRABBEM MMUHDASIN ILLAA ASTAMAU’OOHU WA HUM YALA’ABOONA.\n(There) Cometh not unto them a reminder from their Lord, anew, save they hear it and they get busy in sport.\nلَاهِيَةً قُلُوْبُهُمْ‌ ؕ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّجْوَى‌ۖ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ‌ۖ  هَلْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ‌ ۚ اَفَتَاْتُوْنَ السِّحْرَ وَاَنْتُمْ تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(3)\nLAAHEETAN QULOOBUHUM WAASARROOA AN-NAJWAA LAZEENA ZALAMOO HAL HAAZAA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM AAFATAATOONA SEHR WA ANTUM TUBSEROON.\nPre-occupied at their hearts with trifles; and discoursed in secret; those who did wrong (saying) “Is this (man) other than a human being like unto yourselves; What! will ye then yield unto sorcery while ye see (it)?\nقٰلَ رَبِّىْ يَعْلَمُ الْقَوْلَ فِى السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(4)\nQAALA RABBEE YA’LAMO QAWLA FIL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE WA HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nHe said: “My Lord (well) knoweth (every) word (spoken) in the heaven and the earth; and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.\nبَلْ قَالُوْۤا اَضْغَاثُ اَحْلَامٍۢ بَلِ افْتَرٰٮهُ بَلْ هُوَ شَاعِرٌ ‌ ۖۚ فَلْيَاْتِنَا بِاٰيَةٍ كَمَاۤ اُرْسِلَ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ‏(5)\nBAL QAALOO AAZGHAASU AAHLAAMIN BALIL AFTARAAHU BAL HOWA SHAAE’ERUN FALYAATENAA BE-AAYATIL KAMAA AURSELA AWWALOON.\nNay! say they: (these are) medleys of dreams! Nay! he hath forged it; Nay! he is a poet; let him then bring unto us a sign like unto the ones that were sent unto the former ones (of the apostles).\nمَاۤ اٰمَنَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اَهْلَكْنٰهَا‌ۚ اَفَهُمْ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(6)\nMAA AAAMANAT QABLAHUM MIN QARYATINW AAHLAKNAAHAA AAFAHUM YOAMENOONA.\nBelieved not before them (the people of) any of the towns which We did destroy: what! will these (now) believe?\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ اِلَّا رِجَالًا نُّوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْهِمْ‌ فَسْئَلُوْۤا اَهْلَ الذِّكْرِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(7)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA QABLAKA ILLAA REJAALAN NNOOHEAA ELAYHIM FASALOOA AHLAL AZ-ZEKRE IN KUNTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd We sent not before thee, but men unto whom We did reveal, so ask ye the people of the Reminder if ye know not.\nوَمَا جَعَلْنٰهُمْ جَسَدًا لَّا يَاْكُلُوْنَ الطَّعَامَ وَمَا كَانُوْا خٰلِدِيْنَ‏(8)\nWA MAA JAA’ALNAAHUM JASADAN LAA YAAKOLOON TA-A’AMA WA MAA KAANOO KHAALEDEENA.\nWe made them not (such) bodies not eating the food, and they were not to abide (in this world) for ever.\nثُمَّ صَدَقْنٰهُمُ الْوَعْدَ فَاَنْجَيْنٰهُمْ وَمَنْ نَّشَآءُ وَاَهْلَكْنَا الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(9)\nSUMMA SADAQNAAHUMU AL-WAA’DA FAANJAYNAAHUM WA MAN NNASHAAU WA AHLAKNAL MUSREFEEN.\nThen fulfilled We unto them Our promise (of punishment), then We delivered them, and those whom We willed, and We destroyed the extravagant ones.\nلَقَدْ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكُمْ كِتٰبًا فِيْهِ ذِكْرُكُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(10)\nLAQAD ANZALNAA ELAYKUM KETAABAA FEEHE ZEKRUKUM AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nIndeed have We sent down unto you a Book (the Qur’an) wherein is your remembrance; What! Do ye not then understand?\nوَكَمْ قَصَمْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍ كَانَتْ ظَالِمَةً وَّاَنْشَاْنَا بَعْدَهَا قَوْمًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‏(11)\nWA QASAMNAA MIN QARYATINW KAANAT ZAALEMATAN WWAANSHAANAA BAA’DAHAA QAWMAN AAKHEREEN.\nHow many a town (the people of) which were iniquitous, We did destroy, and raised We up after it another people?\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَحَسُّوْا بَاْسَنَاۤ اِذَا هُمْ مِّنْهَا يَرْكُضُوْنَؕ‏(12)\nFALAMMAA AAHASSOOA BAASANAA EZAA HUM MINHAA YARKUZOONA.\nSo when they felt (the coming of) Our torment, lo! they began (trying) to fly from it.\nلَا تَرْكُضُوْا وَ ارْجِعُوْۤا اِلٰى مَاۤ اُتْرِفْتُمْ فِيْهِ وَمَسٰكِنِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُسْئَلُوْنَ‏(13)\nLAA TARKUZOOA WA ARJEU’OOA ELAA MAA AUTREFTUM FEEHE WAMASAAKENEKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TUS-ALOONA.\n(Said We ): “Flee not ye but return unto that wherein ye revelled, and unto your dwellings, happly ye will be questioned.\nقَالُوْا يٰوَيْلَنَاۤ اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(14)\nQAALOO YAA WAYLANAA INNAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nSaid they: “Oh! Woe unto us! Verily, we were unjust!\nفَمَا زَالَتْ تِّلْكَ دَعْوٰٮهُمْ حَتّٰى جَعَلْنٰهُمْ حَصِيْدًا خٰمِدِيْنَ‏(15)\nFAMAA ZAALAT TTELKA DAA’WAAHUM HATTAA JAA’ALNAAHUM HASEEDAN KHAAMEDEENA.\nAnd ceased not this their cry till We made them like reaped corn, extinct.\nوَمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمَآءَ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا لٰعِبِيْنَ‏(16)\nWA MAA KHALAQNAL SAMAAA-AD WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA LAA-E’BEEN.\nAnd We created not the heavens and the earth and what is between them for sport.\nلَوْ اَرَدْنَاۤ اَنْ نَّتَّخِذَ لَهْوًا لَّا تَّخَذْنٰهُ مِنْ لَّدُنَّاۤ  ۖ  اِنْ كُنَّا فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(17)\nLAW AARADNAA AN NNATTAKHEZA LAHWAN LAA TTAKHAZNAAHU MIN WA IN KUNNAA FAAE’ELEENA.\nHad We intended that We should take amusement, We could certainly have taken it from (the things) with Us, if We had been doing (it) We had willed to do it.\nبَلْ نَقْذِفُ بِالْحَقِّ عَلَى الْبَاطِلِ فَيَدْمَغُهٗ فَاِذَا هُوَ زَاهِقٌ‌ ؕ وَلَكُمُ الْوَيْلُ مِمَّا تَصِفُوْنَ‏(18)\nBALNAQZEFO BIL HAQQE A’LAL BAATELE FAYADMAGHOHU FA-EZAA HOWA ZAAHEQUNW WA LAKOMUL WAYLO MIMMAA TASEFOON.\nNay! We hurl truth upon falsehood, that it crusheth its head, and lo! it vanisheth; and woe unto you for what ye describe (of God).\nوَلَهٗ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَمَنْ عِنْدَهٗ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِهٖ وَلَا يَسْتَحْسِرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(19)\nWA LAHU MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA MAN I’NDAHU LAA YASTAKBEROONA A’N E’EBAADATEH WA LAA YASTAHSEROONA.\nAnd His is whosoever is in the heavens and the earth; and those who are with Him are not proud to worship Him, nor do they get weary.\nيُسَبِّحُوْنَ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ لَا يَفْتُرُوْنَ‏(20)\nYUSABBEHOONA LAYLA WAN NAHAARA LAA YAFTUROONA.\nThey glorify (Him) by night and day, they (even) intermit not.\nاَمِ اتَّخَذُوْۤا اٰلِهَةً مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ هُمْ يُنْشِرُوْنَ‏(21)\nAMIL ATTAKHAZOOA AALEHATAL MENAL ARZE HUM YUNSHEROONA.\nOr have they taken gods from the earth who can raise (the dead)?\nلَوْ كَانَ فِيْهِمَاۤ اٰلِهَةٌ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ لَفَسَدَتَا‌ۚ فَسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَرْشِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَ‏(22)\nLAW KAANA FEEHEMAA AAALEHATUN ILLAA LAAHO LAFASADATAA FA-SUBHAANAL LAAHE RABBE A’RSHIL A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nHad there been in (the heavens and the earth) (other) gods except God, they both had been in disorder; So glorified is God, the Lord of the ‘Arsh’ (High above) from what they attribute (unto Him).\nلَا يُسْئَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْئَلُوْنَ‏(23)\nLAA YUSALO A’MMAA YAF-A’LO WA HUM YUSALOONA.\nHe is not questioned about what He doeth, but they shall be questioned.\nاَمِ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اٰلِهَةً ‌ ؕ قُلْ هَاتُوْا بُرْهَانَكُمْ‌ ۚ هٰذَا ذِكْرُ مَنْ مَّعِىَ وَذِكْرُ مَنْ قَبْلِىْ‌ ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ الْحَقَّ‌ فَهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(24)\nAMIL ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AALEHATAL QUL HAATOO BURHAANAKUM HAAZAA ZEKRU MAN MA-E’YA WAZEKRU MAN QABLEAA BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON HAQQA FAHUM MO’REZOON.\nHave they taken beside Him other gods? Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Bring ye your proof: (that they are gods). This (Qur’an) is the Reminder unto those with me, and the Reminder unto those before me; Nay! most of them know not the truth, so they turn aside.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا نُوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا فَاعْبُدُوْنِ‏(25)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA MIN RASOOLIN ILLAA NOOHEAA ELAYHE ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANAA FA’BODOON.\nAnd sent We not before thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) any apostle but revealed We unto him that “Verily there is no god but I; so worship ye Me (alone)\nوَقَالُوا اتَّخَذَ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَلَدًا‌ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ ؕ بَلْ عِبَادٌ مُّكْرَمُوْنَ ۙ‏(26)\n???\nAnd say they: “The Beneficent (God) hath taken unto Him a son; Glory be to Him! Nay! They are (His) honoured servants.\nلَا يَسْبِقُوْنَهٗ بِالْقَوْلِ وَهُمْ بِاَمْرِهٖ يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(27)\n???\nThey speak not ere He speaketh, and they on His bidding (only) act.\nيَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ وَ لَا يَشْفَعُوْنَۙ اِلَّا لِمَنِ ارْتَضٰى وَهُمْ مِّنْ خَشْيَتِهٖ مُشْفِقُوْنَ‏(28)\n???\nKnoweth He what is before them and what is behind them, and they can not intercede but for him whom He approveth, and they, of His fear, tremble.\nوَمَنْ يَّقُلْ مِنْهُمْ اِنِّىْۤ اِلٰهٌ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ فَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِيْهِ جَهَنَّمَ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA MAN YYAQUL MINHUM INNEE ELAAHUN MIN DOONEHI FA-ZAALEKAL NAJZEEHE JAHANNAM KAZAALEKA NAJZIL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd whosoever of them sayeth; Verily I am god besides Him, such a one will We recompense with hell; Thus do We recompense the iniquitous.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنَّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ كَانَتَا رَتْقًا فَفَتَقْنٰهُمَا‌ ؕ وَجَعَلْنَا مِنَ الْمَآءِ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ حَىٍّ‌ ؕ اَفَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(30)\nAWA LAM YARAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ANNAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA KAANATAA RATQAN FA-FATAQNAAHOMAA, WA JA-A’LNAA MENAL MAAA-E KULLA SHAY-IN HAYY, AFALAA YOAMENOON.\nOr see not those who disbelieve that the heavens and the earth were one piece, and that We clave them asunder; and made We of water everything alive; Will they not then believe?\nوَجَعَلْنَا فِى الْاَرْضِ رَوَاسِىَ اَنْ تَمِيْدَ بِهِمْ وَجَعَلْنَا فِيْهَا فِجَاجًا سُبُلًا لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(31)\nWA JA-A’LNAA FIL ARZE JA-A’LA AN TAMEEDA BEHIM WA JA-A’LNAA FEEHAA FEJAAJAN SUBULAN LA-A’LLAHUM YAHTADOON.\nAnd We have made in the earth, (lofty) mountains (standing firm) lest it should shake with them, and We have made therein broad highways that they may be guided aright.\nوَجَعَلْنَا السَّمَآءَ سَقْفًا مَّحْفُوْظًا ۖۚ وَّهُمْ عَنْ اٰيٰتِهَا مُعْرِضُوْنَ‏(32)\nWA JA-A’LNAA SAMAAA-AD SAQFAN MMAHFOOZAN WA HUM A’N AAAYAATEHAA MUA’REZOONA.\nAnd We have made the heavens a canopy, well guarded; and yet they, from its signs turn aside.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ وَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ‌ؕ كُلٌّ فِىْ فَلَكٍ يَّسْبَحُوْنَ‏(33)\nWA HOWA LAZEE KHALAQAL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA WA SHAMSA WAL QAMARA KULLUL FEE FALAKINY YASBAHOON.\nAnd He it is Who created the night and the day and the sun and the moon; all in their (respective) orbits move (in a swim).\nوَمَا جَعَلْنَا لِبَشَرٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ الْخُلْدَ‌ ؕ اَفَا۟ئِن مِّتَّ فَهُمُ الْخٰلِدُوْنَ‏(34)\nWA MAA JA-A’LNAA LEBASHARIN MIN QABLEKA AL-KHULDA AAFAAEN MMETTA FA HOMUL AL-KHAALEDOONA.\nWe granted not unto any man before thee life eternal, What! then if thou diest, will they live for ever?\nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ذَآئِقَةُ الْمَوْتِ‌ؕ وَنَبْلُوْكُمْ بِالشَّرِّ وَالْخَيْرِ فِتْنَةً‌  ؕ وَاِلَيْنَا تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(35)\nKULLO NAFSIM ZAAA-EQATUL MAWT WANABLOOKUM BEALSSHARRE WA KHAYR FETNATAN WA ELAYNAA TURJA-O’ON.\nEvery soul shall taste of death; We try you with evil and (with) good (by way of) a test; and unto Us shall ye (all) be returned.\nوَاِذَا رَاٰكَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ يَّتَّخِذُوْنَكَ اِلَّا هُزُوًا ؕ اَهٰذَا الَّذِىْ يَذْكُرُ اٰلِهَتَكُمْ‌ۚ وَهُمْ بِذِكْرِ الرَّحْمٰنِ هُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(36)\nWA EZAA RAAKA LAZEENA KAFAROO IN YYATTAKHEZOONAKA ILLAA HOZOWANW AAHAAZAA LAZEE YAZKURU AAALEHATAKUM WA HUM BE-ELAA RAHMAANIR HUM KAAFEROON.\nWhen behold thee those who disbelieve, they take thee not but for a ridicule; (saying) “Is this he who speaketh of your gods?” and (while) they, at the mention of the Beneficent (God), are themselves disbelievers.\nخُلِقَ الْاِنْسَانُ مِنْ عَجَلٍ‌ؕ سَاُورِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِىْ فَلَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنِ‏(37)\nKHOLEQA INSAANO MIN A’AJALIN SAAWREEKUM AAAYAATEAA FALAA TASTAA’JELOONE.\nMan is made of haste; I shall show you My signs, so ask Me not to hasten (on)\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(38)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAA WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd say they: “When will this threat come to pass, if ye be truthful?\nلَوْ يَعْلَمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا حِيْنَ لَا يَكُفُّوْنَ عَنْ وُّجُوْهِهِمُ النَّارَ وَلَا عَنْ ظُهُوْرِهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(39)\nLAW YA’LAMO LAZEENA KAFAROO HEENA LAA YAKUFFOONA A’N WWUJOOHEHEMU NAARAL WA LAA A’N ZOHOOREHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YUNSAROON.\nIf only know those who disbelieve, (of the time) when they shall not be able to keep off from their faces and the backs the (Hell) fire nor shall they be helped.\nبَلْ تَاْتِيْهِمْ بَغْتَةً فَتَبْهَتُهُمْ فَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ رَدَّهَا وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(40)\nBAL TAA-TEEHIM BAGHTATANW FATABHATUHUM FALAA YASTATEE-O’ONA RADDAHAA WA LAA HUM HUM YUNZAROON.\nNay! but it shall come on them suddenly, and make them confounded, so they shall neither be able to repel it, nor will they (then) be respited.\nوَلَقَدِ اسْتُهْزِئَ بِرُسُلٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَحَاقَ بِالَّذِيْنَ سَخِرُوْا مِنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(41)\nLAQADIS ASTUHZEA BERUSULIN MIN QABLEKA FAHAAQA BE-LAZEENA SAKHEROOA MINHUM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd indeed were (also) ridiculed (some) of the apostles before thee, but surrounded those who ridiculed that (very torment) which they had been ridiculing.\nقُلْ مَنْ يَّكْلَؤُكُمْ بِالَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ مِنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ‌ؕ بَلْ هُمْ عَنْ ذِكْرِ رَبِّهِمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(42)\nQUL MAN YYAKLAUKUM BIL-LAYLE WAN NAHAARE MENAL RAHMAAN BAL HUM A’N ELAA RABBEHIM MO’REZOON.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): Who can protect you by night and by day from the Beneficent (God)? Nay! they from the remembrance of their Lord turn aside.\nاَمْ لَهُمْ اٰلِهَةٌ تَمْنَعُهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِنَا ‌ؕ لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ نَصْرَ اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ مِّنَّا يُصْحَبُوْنَ‏(43)\nAM LAHUM AAALEHATUN TAMNAU’UHUM MIN DOONENAA LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA NASRAL ANFOSEHIM WA LAA HUM MINNAA YUSHABOONA.\nOr have they gods who can protect them from Us; They have no power to help their own selves, and nor shall they from Us be protected.\nبَلْ مَتَّعْنَا هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ وَ اٰبَآءَهُمْ حَتّٰى طَالَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْعُمُرُ ‌ؕ اَفَلَا يَرَوْنَ اَنَّا نَاْتِى الْاَرْضَ نَنْقُصُهَا مِنْ اَطْرَافِهَا ؕ‌ اَفَهُمُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(44)\nBAL MATTAA’NAA HAAOOLAAA-E WA AA-BAAA-AHUM HATTAA TAALA A’LAYHEMUL O’MOR AFALAA YARAWNAL ANNAA NAATEAA ARZA NANQUSUHAA MIN AATRAAFEHAA AAFAHUMU GHAALEBOON.\nNay! Provided We (enjoyment) unto these and their fathers until lasted their life; What! See they not that We come unto the land, shortening its borders; Shall they then be the prevailing ones?\nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اُنْذِرُكُمْ بِالْوَحْىِ ‌‌ۖ  وَلَا يَسْمَعُ الصُّمُّ الدُّعَآءَ اِذَا مَا يُنْذَرُوْنَ‏(45)\nQUL INNAMAA AUNZERUKUM BIL-WAHAAE WA LAA YASMA-O’ AS-SUMMU DO-A’AA-A EZAA MAA YUNZAROONA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Verily I do but warn you by the revelation (from God):” But the deaf will hear not whenever they are warned.\nوَلَئِنْ مَّسَّتْهُمْ نَفْحَةٌ مِّنْ عَذَابِ رَبِّكَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ يٰوَيْلَنَاۤ اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA LAIN MMASSATHUM NAFHATUN MIN A’ZAABIN RABBEKA LAYAQOOLUNNAL YAA WAYLANAA INNAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd yet if toucheth them a blast of thy Lord’s punishment, certainly will they say, “Woe unto us! Verily we had been unjust!\nوَنَضَعُ الْمَوَازِيْنَ الْقِسْطَ لِيَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ فَلَا تُظْلَمُ نَفْسٌ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانَ مِثْقَالَ حَبَّةٍ مِّنْ خَرْدَلٍ اَتَيْنَا بِهَا‌ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِنَا حٰسِبِيْنَ‏(47)\nWANAZAU’U AL-MAWAAZEENA AL-QESTA LE-YAWMIL QEYAAMATE FALAA TUZLAMO NAFSUN SHAY-ANW WA KAANA MISQAALA HABBATIN MIN KHARDALIN ATAYNAA BEHAA KAFAA LAKHASAFA HAASEBEENA.\nAnd We shall set up the balances of justice on the Day of Judgment, so no soul shall be dealt with unjustly in the least; and even if there be the weight of a grain of mustard seed, (even that) will We bring it (into account); And sufficient are We (as) reckoners.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ الْفُرْقَانَ وَضِيَآءً وَّذِكْرًا لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(48)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAA WA AALO AL-FURQAANA WAZEEAAAAN WWAZEKRAN LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd indeed We did grant unto Moses and Aaron the (Book of) Criterion (between the right and wrong), and Light and a Reminder for the pious ones.\nالَّذِيْنَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ بِالْغَيْبِ وَهُمْ مِّنَ السَّاعَةِ مُشْفِقُوْنَ‏(49)\nLAZEENA YAKHSHAWNA RABBAHUM BIL-GHAYBE WA HUM MENAL AS-SAAA’ATE MUSHFEQOONA.\nThose who fear their Lord unseen, and of the Hour (of doom) they are frightened.\nوَهٰذَا ذِكْرٌ مُّبٰرَكٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ‌ؕ اَفَاَنْتُمْ لَهٗ مُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(50)\nWA ZIKRUNW MMUBAARAKUN AANZALNAAHU AAFAANTUM LAHU MUNKEROONA.\nAnd this (Qur’an) is a Reminder full of blessings which We have sent it down (Unto Our Apostle Muhammad) Do ye then deny it?\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ رُشْدَهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَ كُنَّا بِهٖ عٰلِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(51)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA IBRAAHEEMA RUSHDAH MIN QABLO WA KUNNAA BEHI A’AALEMEENA.\nAnd indeed gave We unto Abraham his rectitude before, and We did know him well.\nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَا هٰذِهِ التَّمَاثِيْلُ الَّتِىْۤ اَنْتُمْ لَهَا عٰكِفُوْنَ‏(52)\nIZ QAALA LEAABEEHE WA QAWMEHI MAA HAAZEHE AT-TAMAASEELU LATEE ANTUM LAHAA ANTUM.\n(Recollect thou O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when (Abraham) said unto his father and his people: “What are these images unto which ye (as devotees) cleave\nقَالُوْا وَجَدْنَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا لَهَا عٰبِدِيْنَ‏(53)\nQAALOO WAJADNAA AABAAA-ANAA LAHAA A’AABEDEENA.\nSaid they: “Found we our fathers, worshippers unto them\nقَالَ لَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمْ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(54)\nQAALA LAQAD KUNTUM ANTUM WAABAAUKUM FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nSaid he: “Indeed ye and your fathers had been in error manifest.\nقَالُوْۤا اَجِئْتَنَا بِالْحَقِّ اَمْ اَنْتَ مِنَ اللّٰعِبِيْنَ‏(55)\nQAALOO AAJETANAA BIL-HAQQE AM ANTA MENAL AL-LAAE’EBEENA.\nSaid they: “Hast thou brought unto us the truth, or art thou of the jesters?\nقَالَ بَلْ رَّبُّكُمْ رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ الَّذِىْ فَطَرَهُنَّ ‌ۖ  وَاَنَا عَلٰى ذٰلِكُمْ مِّنَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(56)\nQAALA BAL RRABBUKUM RABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LAZEE FATARAHUNNA ANAT A’LAA ZAALEKUM MENAL SHAAHEDEEN.\nSaid he: “Nay! Your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, Who hath created them; and I am unto this, one of the witnesses.\nوَ تَاللّٰهِ لَاَكِيْدَنَّ اَصْنَامَكُمْ بَعْدَ اَنْ تُوَلُّوْا مُدْبِرِيْنَ‏(57)\nWA TAALLLAAHE LAAKEEDANNA AASNAAMAKUM BA’DA AN TOWALLOO MUDBEREEN.\nAnd by God, I will scheme against your idols after ye go away, turning back\nفَجَعَلَهُمْ جُذٰذًا اِلَّا كَبِيْرًا لَّهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ اِلَيْهِ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(58)\nFA-JA-A’LAHUM JUZAAZAN ILLAA KABEERAA LAHUM LA-A’LLAHUM ELAYHE YARJE-O’ON.\nSo he broke them into pieces, except the chief of them, that happly they may unto him return.\nقَالُوْا مَنْ فَعَلَ هٰذَا بِاٰلِهَتِنَاۤ اِنَّهٗ لَمِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(59)\nQAALOO MAN FA-A’LA HAAZAA BEAAALEHATENAA INNAHU LAMENAS ZAALEMEEN.\nSaid they: “Who hath done this to our gods? Verily he is of the unjust ones\nقَالُوْا سَمِعْنَا فَتًى يَّذْكُرُهُمْ يُقَالُ لَهٗۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمُ ؕ‏(60)\nQAALOO SAMEA’NAA FATAN YYAZKURUHUM YOQAALO LAHU AEBRAAHEEMU.\n(Some others) said: “We heard a youth speak of them, he is called Abraham\nقَالُوْا فَاْتُوْا بِهٖ عَلٰٓى اَعْيُنِ النَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْهَدُوْنَ‏(61)\nQAALOO FAATOO BEHI A’LAA AAA’YUNE NAASE LA-A’LLAHUM YASHHADOONA.\nThey said: “Then bring him before the eyes of the people, that they may bear witness.\nقَالُوْٓا ءَاَنْتَ فَعَلْتَ هٰذَا بِاٰلِهَتِنَا يٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُؕ‏(62)\nA-TAJ-A’LO AANTA FAA’ALTA HAAZAA BEAAALEHATENAA YAABRAAHEEMU.\nSaid they: “Hast thou done this to our gods, O’ Abraham?\nقَالَ بَلْ فَعَلَهٗ ‌‌ۖ  كَبِيْرُهُمْ هٰذَا فَسْئَلُوْهُمْ اِنْ كَانُوْا يَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(63)\nQAALA BAL FAA’ALAH KABEERUHUM HAAZAA FASALOOHUM IN KAANOO YANTEQOON.\n(Abraham) said: “Nay! Hath done it he, the chief of them is this (idol) so ye ask them, if they can speak\nفَرَجَعُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ فَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّكُمْ اَنْتُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَۙ‏(64)\nFARAJAU’OOA ELAA ANFOSEHIM FA-QAALOO INNAKUM AANTUMU ZAALEMOON.\nThen they turned unto them selves and said, “Verily, ye are yourselves the unjust ones,\nثُمَّ نُكِسُوْا عَلٰى رُءُوْسِہِمْ‌ۚ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَا هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ يَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(65)\nSUMMA NUKESOOA A’LAA RUOOSEM LAQAD A’ALEMTA MAA HAAOOLAAA-E YANTEQOON.\nThen they were confounded in their heads, (and they helplessly said): “Thou knowest fully well that these (idols) speak not!\nقَالَ اَفَتَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَضُرُّكُمْؕ‏(66)\nQAALA AAFATAA’BUDOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFAU’UKUM SHAY-ANW WA LAA YAZURRUKUM.\nSaid: (Abraham) “What! worship ye then besides God what profiteth you not, nor do any harm unto you?\nاُفٍّ لَّكُمْ وَلِمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(67)\nAUFFIN LAKUM WA LEMAKH TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAH AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nFie on you and on what ye worship besides God. What! Do ye not understand?\nقَالُوْا حَرِّقُوْهُ وَانْصُرُوْۤا اٰلِهَتَكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(68)\nQAALOO HARREQOOHU WAANSUROOA AAALEHATAKUM IN KUNTUM FAAE’ELEENA.\nSaid they: “Burn him and help your gods, if ye can do (anything at all);\nقُلْنَا يٰنَارُ كُوْنِىْ بَرْدًا وَّسَلٰمًا عَلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَۙ‏(69)\nQULNAL YAA NAARUL KOONEAA BARDANW WWASALAAMAN A’LAA IBRAAHEEMA.\nSaid We; “O’ fire! Be thou cold, and a safety unto Abraham,\nوَاَرَادُوْا بِهٖ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنٰهُمُ الْاَخْسَرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(70)\nWAARAADOOA BEHI KAYDAANW FAJAA’ALNAAHUMU AL-AAKHSAREENA.\nAnd they intended a device against him, but We made them the greatest losers,\nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَلُوْطًا اِلَى الْاَرْضِ الَّتِىْ بٰرَكْنَا فِيْهَا لِلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(71)\nWANAJJAYNAAHU WA LOOTAN ELAL ARZE LATEE BAARAKNAA FEEHAA LIL-A’AALAMEENA.\nAnd We delivered him and (also) Lot, (and took them safely) to the land which We have blessed for all worlds.\nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ ؕ وَيَعْقُوْبَ نَافِلَةً‌  ؕ وَكُلًّا جَعَلْنَا صٰلِحِيْنَ‏(72)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA NAAFELATAN WAKULLAN JA-A’LNAA SAALEHEENA.\nAnd We gave him Isaac, and Jacob, as a further gift, and made We all of them righteous ones.\nوَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَئِمَّةً يَّهْدُوْنَ بِاَمْرِنَا وَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمْ فِعْلَ الْخَيْرٰتِ وَاِقَامَ الصَّلٰوةِ وَاِيْتَآءَ الزَّكٰوةِ‌ۚ وَكَانُوْا لَنَا عٰبِدِيْنَ ۙ‌ۚ‏(73)\nWA JA-A’LNAAHUM AIMMATAWN YYAHDOONA BEAAMRENAA WA AWHAYNAA ELAYHIM FEA’LA AL-KHAYRAATE WAAQAAMA AS-SALAAWTE WAAYTAAA AZ-ZAKAAWTE WA KAANOO LANAA A’AABEDEENA.\nAnd We made them leaders, guiding (the people) by Our command, and revealed We unto them the doing of good, and the establishing of prayer, and the giving of alms, and (only) unto Us did they worship,\nوَلُوْطًا اٰتَيْنٰهُ حُكْمًا وَّعِلْمًا وَّنَجَّيْنٰهُ مِنَ الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِىْ كَانَتْ تَّعْمَلُ الْخَبٰٓئِثَ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمَ سَوْءٍ فٰسِقِيْنَۙ‏(74)\nWA LOOTAN AATAYNAAHO HUKMAWN WA I’LMAA WWANAJJAYNAAHU MENAL QARYAH LATEE KAANAT TTAA’MALU AL-KHABAAAESA INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMA SAWIN FAASEQEEN.\nAnd Lot, We gave him wisdom, the knowledge; and We delivered him from the town which were doing filthiness; for they were people evil, perverse,\nوَاَدْخَلْنٰهُ فِىْ رَحْمَتِنَا‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(75)\nWAADKHALNAAHU FEE RAHMATENAA INNAHU MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd We admitted him into Our mercy; verily he was of the righteous ones.\nوَنُوْحًا اِذْ نَادٰى مِنْ قَبْلُ فَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗ فَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗ مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(76)\nWA ARSALNAA IZ NAADAA MIN QABLO FAASTAJABNAA LAHU FANAJJAYNAAHU AHLAHU MENAL AL-KARBE A’ZEEM.\nAnd (remember) Noah, when he cried aforetime, then We responded unto him and delivered him and his companions from the great calamity.\nوَنَصَرْنٰهُ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمَ سَوْءٍ فَاَغْرَقْنٰهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(77)\nWANASARNAAHU MENAL QAWMIL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMA SAWIN FAAGHRAQNAAHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nAnd We helped him against his people who belied Our signs; verily they were an evil people, so We drowned them all.\nوَدَاوٗدَ وَسُلَيْمٰنَ اِذْ يَحْكُمٰنِ فِى الْحَرْثِ اِذْ نَفَشَتْ فِيْهِ غَنَمُ الْقَوْمِ‌ۚ وَكُنَّا لِحُكْمِهِمْ شٰهِدِيْنَ ۙ‏(78)\nWA DAAWOODA WA SOLAYMAANA IZ YAHKUMAANE FIL AL-HARSE IZ NAFASHAT FEEHE GHANAMU QAWMIL KUNNAA LEHUKMEHEM SHAAHEDEENA.\nAnd David and Solomon when they were judging about the corn-field when the sheep of the people pastured in it by night, and We unto their judgment were among the witnesses,\nفَفَهَّمْنٰهَا سُلَيْمٰنَ‌‌ۚ وَكُلًّا اٰتَيْنَا حُكْمًا وَّعِلْمًا‌ وَّسَخَّرْنَا مَعَ دَاوٗدَ الْجِبَالَ يُسَبِّحْنَ وَالطَّيْرَ‌ ؕ وَكُنَّا فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(79)\nFAFAHHAMNAAHAA SOLAYMAANA WAKULLAN AATAYNAA HUKMAWN WA I’LMAA WWASAKKHARNAA LAAHA DAAWOODA JEBAALA YUSABBEHNA WA TAYRA KUNNAA FAAE’ELEENA.\nThen We made Solomon to understand it; and unto each one gave We wisdom and knowledge, and We made subservient with David the mountains and the birds; to sing hymns of (Our praise) And We were the doers.\nوَعَلَّمْنٰهُ صَنْعَةَ لَبُوْسٍ لَّكُمْ لِتُحْصِنَكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَاْسِكُمْ‌ۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ شٰكِرُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA A’LLAMNAAHUSH-SHE’RA SANA’ATA LABOOSIN LAKUM LETUHSENAKUM MIN BAASEKUM FA HAL ANTUM SHAAKEROONA.\nAnd We taught him the art of making the coat of mail for you that ye might protect yourselves in your wars; Will ye then be grateful?\nوَلِسُلَيْمٰنَ الرِّيْحَ عَاصِفَةً تَجْرِىْ بِاَمْرِهٖۤ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ الَّتِىْ بٰرَكْنَا فِيْهَا‌ؕ وَكُنَّا بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عٰلِمِيْنَ‏(81)\nWA LESOLAYMAANA AR-REEHA A’AASEFATAN TAJREE LAAHO ELAL ARZE LATEE BAARAKNAA FEEHAA KUNNAA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’AALEMEENA.\nAnd unto Solomon (We subjected) the wind blowing violent, blowing at his command unto the land wherein We had blessed; And We are, of all things the Knowers.\nوَمِنَ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ مَنْ يَّغُوْصُوْنَ لَهٗ وَيَعْمَلُوْنَ عَمَلًا دُوْنَ ذٰ لِكَ‌ ۚ وَكُنَّا لَهُمْ حٰفِظِيْنَۙ‏(82)\nWA MENAN ASH-SHAYTEENE MAN YYAGHOOSOONA LAHU WA YA’MALOON A’AMALAN DOONA ZAA LEKA KUNNAA LAHUM HAAFEZEEN.\nAnd of the satans there were those who used to dive for him and to do other work besides that; and We were guardians over them,\nوَاَيُّوْبَ اِذْ نَادٰى رَبَّهٗۤ اَنِّىْ مَسَّنِىَ الضُّرُّ وَاَنْتَ اَرْحَمُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(83)\nWAAYYOOBA IZ NAADAA WAL AANNEAA MASSANEAAA AZ-ZURRU WA ANTA AARHAMU AR-RAAHEMEENA.\nAnd (Remember) Job (Ayyub), when he cried unto his Lord (saying); “Verily hath touched me distress, and Thou art the Most Merciful of the merciful ones!\nفَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗ فَكَشَفْنَا مَا بِهٖ مِنْ ضُرٍّ‌ وَّاٰتَيْنٰهُ اَهْلَهٗ و مِثْلَهُمْ مَّعَهُمْ رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِنَا وَذِكْرٰى لِلْعٰبِدِيْنَ‏(84)\nFAASTAJABNAA LAHU FAKASHAFNAA MAA BEHI MIN ZURRIN WWAATAYNAAHU AHLAHU W MESLAHUM MMAA’AHUM RAHMATAM MIN I’NDENAA WAZEKRAA LIL-A’AABEDEENA.\nSo We responded unto him and We removed what he was distressed with, and We gave him and his family and the like of them with them, a mercy from unto Us, and a reminder unto the worshippers (of Ours).\nوَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِدْرِيْسَ وَذَا الْكِفْلِ‌ؕ كُلٌّ مِّنَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(85)\nWA ISMAA-E’ELA WAADREESA WA ZAL AL-KEFLE KULLUL MENAL MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nAnd (remember) Ishmael and Idris and Dhul-Kifl; all were of the patient ones.\nوَاَدْخَلْنٰهُمْ فِىْ رَحْمَتِنَا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(86)\nWAADKHALNAAHUM FEE RAHMATENAA INNAHUM MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd We admitted them into Our Mercy; Verily they were of the righteous.\nوَ ذَا النُّوْنِ اِذْ ذَّهَبَ مُغَاضِبًا فَظَنَّ اَنْ لَّنْ نَّقْدِرَ عَلَيْهِ فَنَادٰى فِى الظُّلُمٰتِ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ سُبْحٰنَكَ ‌ۖ  اِنِّىْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(87)\nWA ZAL AN-NOONE IZ ZZAHABA MUGHAAZEBAN FA ZANNAS AN LAN-Y NNAQDERA A’LAYHE FANAADAA FIL ZOLOMAATE AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA INNEE KUNTO MENAL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd (remember) Yunus i.e. Zunnun when went he in anger, and imagined he that never would We straiten him; Then he cried out from the darkness: “There is no god but “Thou (O’ my Lord!), Glory be to Thee, verily I was of the unjust ones!\nفَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗۙ وَنَجَّيْنٰهُ مِنَ الْغَمِّ‌ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نُنْجِى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(88)\nFAASTAJABNAA LAHU WANAJJAYNAAHU MENAL AL-GHAMME WA KAZAALEKA NUNJEAA MOAMENEEN.\nThen responded We unto him and delivered him from the grief, thus do We deliver the believers.\nوَزَكَرِيَّاۤ اِذْ نَادٰى رَبَّهٗ رَبِّ لَا تَذَرْنِىْ فَرْدًا وَّاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْوٰرِثِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(89)\nWA ZAKARIYYAA IZ NAADAA RABBAHU RABBE LAA TAZARNEE FARDANW WA ANTA KHAYRUL WAARESEEN.\nAnd (remember) Zachariah, when he cried unto his Lord: “O’ my Lord! Leave me not alone (without an issue) though Thou art the Best of heirs!\nفَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗ وَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗ يَحْيٰى وَاَصْلَحْنَا لَهٗ زَوْجَهٗ ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا يُسٰرِعُوْنَ فِىْ الْخَيْرٰتِ وَ يَدْعُوْنَنَا رَغَبًا وَّرَهَبًا ‌ؕ وَكَانُوْا لَنَا خٰشِعِيْنَ‏(90)\nFAASTAJABNAA LAHU WA WAHABNAA LAHU YAHYAA WAASLAHNAA LAHU ZAWJAH INNAHUM KAANOO YUSAAREU’OONA FEE AL-KHAYRAATE WA YADU’OONANAA RAGHABAN WWARAHABAN WA KAANOO LANAA KHAASHEE’EENA.\nThen responded We unto him and gifted unto him John (Yahya), and adjusted his wife (of her barrenness) for him; verily, they did vie in goodness and did call unto Us, with love and reverence, and were unto Us humbled\nوَالَّتِىْۤ اَحْصَنَتْ فَرْجَهَا فَنَفَخْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ رُّوْحِنَا وَ جَعَلْنٰهَا وَابْنَهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(91)\nWA LATEE AAHSANAT FARJAHAA FANAFAKHNAA FEEHAA MIN RROOHENAA WA JA-A’LNAAHAA WAABNAHAA AAYATAL LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad! remember) her (Mary) who guarded her chastity We breathed into her Our Spirit, and We made her and her son a sign unto all peoples.\nاِنَّ هٰذِهٖۤ اُمَّتُكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً  ‌ۖ وَّاَنَا رَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْنِ‏(92)\nINNAL HAAZEHI AUMMATUKUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN WWAANAA RABBOKUM FA’BODOON.\nVerily, this (Islam) is your group, one group and I am your Lord! therefore worship ye Me (alone)!\nوَتَقَطَّعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ كُلٌّ اِلَيْنَا رٰجِعُوْنَ‏(93)\nWATAQATTAU’OOA AAMRAHUM BAYNAHUM KULLUL ELAYNAA RAAJE-O’ON.\nBut they have rent asunder (this) their concern among them selves (into sects), (and yet) unto Us shall all of them return.\nفَمَنْ يَّعْمَلْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَلَا كُفْرَانَ لِسَعْيِهٖ‌ۚ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ كٰتِبُوْنَ‏(94)\nFAMAN YA’MAL MENAL SAALEHAATE WA HOWA MUMENUN FALAA KUFRAANA LESAA’YEH WA INNAA LAHU KAATEBOONA.\nSo whosoever shall do of good deeds and he be a believer, there shall not be any rejection of his endeavour, and verily, We will write it down for him.\nوَ حَرٰمٌ عَلٰى قَرْيَةٍ اَهْلَكْنٰهَاۤ اَنَّهُمْ لَا يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(95)\nWA HARAAMUN A’LAA QARYATINW AAHLAKNAAHAA ANNAHUM LAA YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd is forbidden unto (the people of) the towns which We did destroy that they shall not return.\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا فُتِحَتْ يَاْجُوْجُ وَمَاْجُوْجُ وَهُمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ حَدَبٍ يَّنْسِلُوْنَ‏(96)\nHATTAA EZAA FUTEHAT YAAJOOJU WAMAAJOOJU WA HUM MIN KULLE HADABIN YYANSELOONA.\nUntil are let loose the Gog and the Magog and they shall from every elevation hasten forth.\nوَاقْتَرَبَ الْوَعْدُ الْحَقُّ فَاِذَا هِىَ شَاخِصَةٌ اَبْصَارُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ يٰوَيْلَنَا قَدْ كُنَّا فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ هٰذَا بَلْ كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(97)\nWAAQTARABA WA’DO HAQQO FA-EZAA HEYA SHAAKHESATUN AABSAARU LAZEENA KAFAROO YAA WAYLANAA QAD KUNNAA FEE GHAFLATIM MIN HAAZAA BAL KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd the true promise shall draw nigh, then lo! stare amazedly, the eyes of those who disbelieve; (and they shall say): “Woe unto us! Indeed were we in heedlessness as to this; Nay! we were unjust ones.\nاِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ حَصَبُ جَهَنَّمَؕ اَنْتُمْ لَهَا وَارِدُوْنَ‏(98)\nINNAKUM WA MAA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE HASABU JAHANNAM ANTUM LAHAA WAAREDOONA.\nVerily, ye and what ye worship beside God, shall be the fuel for hell; unto ye shall arrive.\nلَوْ كَانَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اٰلِهَةً مَّا وَرَدُوْهَا‌ ؕ وَكُلٌّ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(99)\nLAW KAANA HAAOOLAAA-E AALEHATAL MAA WARADOOHAA KULLUN FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nWere these been gods they would not have come unto it and all shall abide therein.\nلَهُمْ فِيْهَا زَفِيْرٌ وَّهُمْ فِيْهَا لَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(100)\nLAHUM FEEHAA ZAFEERUN WA HUM FEEHAA LAA YAS-MA-O’ONA.\nFor them therein shall be groaning, and they therein shall not hear (any other sound)\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ سَبَقَتْ لَهُمْ مِّنَّا الْحُسْنٰٓىۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ عَنْهَا مُبْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(101)\nINNAL LAZEENA SABAQAT LAHUM MINNAA AL-HUSNAAA OOLAAA-EKA A’NHAA MUBA’ADOONA.\nVerily those for whom hath went forth from Us goodness, those from it (Hell) shall be kept away,\nلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ حَسِيْسَهَا‌ ۚ وَهُمْ فِىْ مَا اشْتَهَتْ اَنْفُسُهُمْ خٰلِدُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(102)\nLAA YAS-MA-O’ONA HASEESAHAA WA HUM FEE MAA ASHTAHAT ANFOSOHUM KHAALEDOON.\nThey will hear not (even) the slightest sound of it (Hell), and they in what their souls desire, shall abide.\nلَا يَحْزُنُهُمُ الْفَزَعُ الْاَكْبَرُ وَتَتَلَقّٰٮهُمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ ؕ هٰذَا يَوْمُكُمُ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(103)\nLAA YAHZUNUHUMU AL-FAZAU’U AL-AAKBARU WATATALAQQAAHUMU TAHMELOHUL HAAZAA YAWMUKUMU LAZEE KUNTUM TOO-A’DOON.\nShall grieve them not the great terror and the angels shall meet them (saying): “This is your Day, which ye were promised\nيَوْمَ نَطْوِىْ السَّمَآءَ كَطَىِّ السِّجِلِّ لِلْكُتُبِ‌ ؕ كَمَا بَدَاْنَاۤ اَوَّلَ خَلْقٍ نُّعِيْدُهٗ‌ ؕ وَعْدًا عَلَيْنَا‌ ؕ اِنَّا كُنَّا فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(104)\nYAWMA NATWEAA SAMAAA-AD KATAA AS-SEJELLE LIL-KUTUBE KAMAA BADAANAA AWWALA KHALQIN NNUE’EEDUH WA’DAN A’LAYNAA INNAA KUNNAA FAAE’ELEENA.\nOn that day will We roll up the heaven, as is rolled up the written scroll; As we caused the first creation, so will We get it return. (It is) a promise binding Us, Verily We were doing it.\nوَلَقَدْ كَتَبْنَا فِى الزَّبُوْرِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الذِّكْرِ اَنَّ الْاَرْضَ يَرِثُهَا عِبَادِىَ الصّٰلِحُوْنَ‏(105)\nWA LAQAD KATABNAA FIL AZ-ZABOORE MIN BA’DE AZ-ZEKRE ANNAL ARZA YARESUHAA E’EBAADEAAA AS-SAALEHOONA.\nAnd indeed We did write in the Psalms (Zabur) (given to David) after the Reminder (at-Tawrat given to Moses), that the earth, shall inherit it My servants righteous.\nاِنَّ فِىْ هٰذَا لَبَلٰغًا لِّقَوْمٍ عٰبِدِيْنَؕ‏(106)\nINNAL FEE HAAZAA LABALAAGHAN LEQAWMINY A’AABEDEENA.\nVerily in this is a conveyance for a people who worship (Us).\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا رَحْمَةً لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(107)\nWA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA RAHMATAM LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd We sent thee not (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) but a Mercy unto (all) the worlds.\nقُلْ اِنَّمَا يُوْحٰۤى اِلَىَّ اَنَّمَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ‌  ۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(108)\nQUL INNAMAA YOOHAA ELAYYA ANNAMAA ELAAHOKUM ELAAHUN WAAHED FA HAL ANTUM MUSLEMOON.\nSay: “It hath only been revealed unto me that your God is One God: Will ye then submit (unto Him i.e. be Muslims)\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقُلْ اٰذَنْتُكُمْ عَلٰى سَوَآءٍ ‌ؕ وَاِنْ اَدْرِىْۤ اَقَرِيْبٌ اَمْ بَعِيْدٌ مَّا تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(109)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FAQUL AAAZANTUKUM A’LAA SAWAAIN WA AADREAA AAQAREEBUN AM BAE’EEDUN MAA TOO-A’DOON.\nAnd if they turn back say: “I have warned you all alike; and I know not whether nigh or far, is that which ye are promised.\nاِنَّهٗ يَعْلَمُ الْجَهْرَ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تَكْتُمُوْنَ‏(110)\nINNAHU YA’LAMO JAHRA MENAL AL-QAWLE YA’LAMO MAA TAKTOMOON.\nVerily, He knoweth what is spoken aloud, and He knoweth (too) what ye hide\nوَاِنْ اَدْرِىْ لَعَلَّهٗ فِتْنَةٌ لَّكُمْ وَمَتَاعٌ اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(111)\nWA AADREAA LA-A’LLAHU FITNATUN LAKUM WA LIL-MOTAALLAQAATE ELAA HEEN.\nAnd I know not (also) happly this (respite) may be a trial for you and a provision until a time.\nقٰلَ رَبِّ احْكُمْ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ وَرَبُّنَا الرَّحْمٰنُ الْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلٰى مَا تَصِفُوْنَ‏(112)\nQAALA RABBE AHKUM BIL-HAQ WA RABBONAA RAHMAANO AL-MUSTAA’AANU A’LAA MAA TASEFOONA.\nSaid (the Apostle Muhammad praying): “O’ my Lord! Judge Thou with truth; And Our Lord is the Beneficent, Whose help is sought against what ye ascribe (unto Him)",
  "merits": "Surah al-Anbiyaa (The Prophets)\nThis ‘Makki’ Surah has 112 verses. It is narrated that the reward for reciting this Surah is that the accounting on the Day of Reckoning becomes easy for the reciter and all the Prophets whose names appear in the Holy Qur’an will come to meet him on this day.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites Surah al-Anbiyaa frequently, his status in Paradise will be close to the Prophets. Writing this Surah and keeping it with one removes all stress and worry."
}
